OpenKai2

The native runtime uses PS2Recomp by ran-j and contributors:
https://github.com/ran-j/PS2Recomp

The build tools target PS2Recomp revision
eb8688b2fd191129f103a39543002c005b33409c, licensed under GNU GPL version 3.
PS2Recomp and its dependencies are downloaded during setup. Their copyright
notices and licenses remain applicable.

The VU1 native recompiler and reference interpreter use PCSX2's microVU and
vector core by the PCSX2 Dev Team, revision
dcfd663c1903025864a865d3fcf508d0caab70c7 (v2.1.27):
https://github.com/PCSX2/pcsx2
These sources retain their LGPL-3.0-or-later notices and are included under
third_party/pcsx2-vu/. Their fast_float headers use the MIT license. The
application and integration code remain GPL-3.0-only. The bundled fmt 12.1.0
formatting headers retain their MIT license.

Game audio is synthesized by PCSX2's SPU2 core from the same revision,
included under third_party/pcsx2-spu2/ with its LGPL-3.0-or-later notices.

The spatial presentation upscaler uses AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1,
revision a21ffb8f6c13233ba336352bdff293894c706575:
https://github.com/GPUOpen-Effects/FidelityFX-FSR
The unmodified shader headers in third_party/fidelityfx-fsr/ retain their MIT
notices, including Michal Drobot's shader portability contributions. This is
FSR 1 spatial upscaling, without temporal reconstruction or frame generation.

The launcher's display lettering uses Bangers by Vernon Adams and the Bangers
Project Authors, from google/fonts revision
9b59ea9f333c5b8a99fa44e2a698496d6cde5b8e, licensed under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1. The unmodified font and its license are in third_party/bangers/
and are embedded in the launcher.

Portable Windows bundles include third-party notices in licenses/. The source
locations for those notices and the pinned FFmpeg build recipe are recorded in
third_party/licenses/sources.json.

Dragon Ball Z: Budokai 2 content and trademarks belong to their respective
rights holders. Original game executables, disc images, and disc assets are
not supplied. The native runtime requires the user's original USA ISO.

Music time stretching uses SoundTouch by Olli Parviainen, licensed under
LGPL-2.1-or-later. Its source and license are in third_party/soundtouch.
